                "word": "Chappy",
                "pos": "name",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3d6d4707-a859-3f69-9057-7454133718d2",
                        "entry_id": "95aa8cec-6703-3d01-a903-7a8e1483e838",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Clipping of Chappaquiddick Island: an island of Dukes County, Massachusetts, United States, east of Martha's Vineyard."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "abbreviation",
                            "alt-of",
                            "clipping",
                            "colloquial"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8ea41a41-e6d0-41dc-aa5c-fe6f53502454",
                                "sense_id": "3d6d4707-a859-3f69-9057-7454133718d2",
                                "text": "But reality is change, so new houses and people were appearing on Chappy as on the rest of the Vineyard, and they would continue to appear; the old days were gone with the wind, like the antebellum South."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cf85e748-bb85-46d7-b91f-c7be2a587b05",
                                "sense_id": "3d6d4707-a859-3f69-9057-7454133718d2",
                                "text": "A more recent second breach has created an additional tiny island between the Vineyard and Chappy, further separating us and increasing the tenderness of the southern shore."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "88305009-2697-4359-b530-4b538e041a3f",
                                "sense_id": "3d6d4707-a859-3f69-9057-7454133718d2",
                                "text": "Because it's the only method of transportation between the two islands and a surprising number of people live on Chappy year-round, the ferry runs daily."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
